{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788271319,"nonce":"6qKo/LByOPXZfcr/a9OmEamdrEo=","message":"SEQUENCED — Evan, 2026-09-01: **this issue is held until after M2, and it is the\nfirst thing after it.**\n\nThat is not new; it is comment #1's ruling honoured. The round that makes\nblueprints buildable had scheduled this as a parallel session on the grounds\nthat it touches no C# and so does not contend for the single DLL. That is a\nRESOURCE argument and it says nothing about whether the work should happen yet.\nEvan's framing when it came up: *\"c should be held off until the normal way is\nproven.\"*\n\n**The acceptance already said the same thing, and nobody had noticed.** Three of\nits five bullets cannot be satisfied before `place-layout` exists:\n\n- \"`place-layout` REFUSES an off-phase origin with a reason naming the phase it\n  expected\" — there is no `place-layout`.\n- \"Two adjacent modules placed in sequence share their common wall: built once,\n  billed once, both rooms read as enclosed\" — needs `place-layout` and a bench.\n- \"A rehearsal places at least a 2x2 block of modules and the result is a\n  connected base\" — same.\n\nThe two that ARE reachable today are \"record the module size and subdivision\nvocabulary in DESIGN\" and \"re-cut or mark the three templates\". Doing those\nalone would re-cut the corpus to a module nobody has ever placed, and leave the\nissue open on its three real bullets — which is the worst of both.\n\n\nSession 14 discharged the prerequisite this issue named. **Row 0 is north,\npinned** (`b4d1f04`) — in `templates/INDEX.md`, in `ir.py`'s own docstring, in\nDESIGN's decisions log and in all three template diagrams. Comment #2 above said\nphase is meaningless without a fixed orientation; it now has one.\n\nThe pin also found a real corpus bug, which is worth knowing before re-cutting\nanything: `freezer-kitchen` carried `FueledStove_South`, whose interaction cell\nlands in the north wall, because the rotation suffix had been documented as \"the\ndirection the def FACES\" — a gloss that means opposite things for a cooler and a\nworkbench. Pin 2 is now the `Rot4` value verbatim. **Check the corpus against\nthe module the same way when you re-cut it**: against the rule, not against the\nassumption that it already complies.\n\n\nThe 7x7 module, subdivision vocabulary (quarter, half, corner) as IR rather than\nprose, shared-wall ownership and the double-billing question, the off-phase\nrefusal, and re-cutting or marking the three templates. Plus the hazard from\nyour own body: on a grid a one-cell placement slide is CUMULATIVE and silently\nde-phases every module after it, so `acee526` (1.9, exact-or-refuse) is\nload-bearing here even though it does not block the first room.","files":null}]}